  "ingredients": [
    "1 1/2 cup cheddar cheese (shredded)",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
    "6 ounce bacon",
    "6 large egg",
    "1 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "6 tablespoon salsa"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. Start by placing the cheese in piles (equal to serving totals) on a Silpat. I prefer to use Silpats because they are nonstick and cheese cooks very well on them. Season the cheese piles with paprika and cayenne pepper and bake for 10–12 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immediately after taking them out of the oven, use an upside-down cupcake tray to form half of the crisps into a cup-like shape. Set these aside for later.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thinly slice the bacon and add it to a heated pan. Cook until crisp. Once browned, remove the bacon from the pan, reserving as much of the grease as possible.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the strips of bacon on a paper towel to crisp up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry half of the eggs in the bacon grease. Use a small ramekin or egg ring to cut off the egg whites and create a perfect circular egg. Once these eggs are finished, scramble the other eggs in the remaining bacon fat. Season them well and don't overcook them!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the fried eggs to the flat cheese crisps and the scrambled eggs to the cup-shaped crisps. Top with bacon and salsa.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets-13.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/egg-bacon-cheese-baskets/#wprm-recipe-50773-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
